    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0269" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 113 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Truman
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d113-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-01">1 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Truman. Personal, private and top secret. No. 99.</p>
                <p>Your Number 76.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d113-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The King has now decided he must visit Ulster in the period during the Berlin
                    conference and therefore your kind telegram on this subject would have no
                    application. You will no doubt have received His Majesty’s invitation to visit
                    this island.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d113-f3"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d113-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d113-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels. <ref
                        target="#d71">Document No. 71</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f2" n="2" xml:id="d113-f2-content">
